// This file tracks known vulnerabilities that are accepted or mitigated.
// It is the enforcement source of truth for the CI vulnerability gate: every
// vulnerability ID listed here is exempted from blocking CI, provided the
// waiver carries a justification, a future review date, an owner, and a
// status. CI fails the build when a waiver is expired, malformed, or
// ownerless.
// Review date format: YYYY-MM-DD

// GO-2026-4316: Open redirect vulnerability in github.com/go-chi/chi
// Justification:
// - RedirectSlashes middleware is not used in our codebase
// - Dependency is transitive through github.com/stellar/go-stellar-sdk
// - No fix available yet (Fixed in: N/A)
// - Code review confirmed middleware is not invoked
// Review date: 2027-01-01
// Owner: security-team
// Status: Accepted - waiting for upstream fix
GO-2026-4316

// GO-2026-5037: Inefficient candidate hostname parsing in crypto/x509 (stdlib)
// Justification:
// - CPU-exhaustion issue triggered by parsing untrusted certificates; the API
//   only parses certificates from trusted counterparties, and TLS is handled
//   by the standard library with default validation
// - Fixed in Go 1.25.11 / 1.26.4; CI toolchain (go.mod: 1.25.12) is already
//   patched, waiver retained for older local toolchains pending upgrade
// Review date: 2026-12-01
// Owner: security-team
// Status: Accepted - fixed in Go 1.25.11+; pending toolchain upgrade
GO-2026-5037

// GO-2026-5039: Arbitrary inputs included in errors without escaping in
// net/textproto (stdlib)
// Justification:
// - Error-message injection in header parsing; affects debug/log output only,
//   no secret material is echoed and no transport-level impact for our usage
// - Fixed in Go 1.25.11 / 1.26.4; CI toolchain (go.mod: 1.25.12) is already
//   patched, waiver retained for older local toolchains pending upgrade
// Review date: 2026-12-01
// Owner: security-team
// Status: Accepted - fixed in Go 1.25.11+; pending toolchain upgrade
GO-2026-5039
